WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.910
My final exam was all calculations.

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:08.490
My best students got top marks, then in

3
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.850
their first internship they could not

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.050
decide which analysis a real question

5
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:14.510
needed.

6
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.420
I had taught the tools, not the judgement.

7
00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.710
Today: how to align a statistics or

8
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.470
data-science module, design real

9
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.330
projects, require reproducible work,

10
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.710
and grade it fairly with a rubric.

11
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.350
Biggs calls it constructive alignment.

12
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.680
Write the learning outcomes first, using

13
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.100
verbs like analyse and justify.

14
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.460
Then choose activities that practise those

15
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.640
verbs, and assessments that measure them.

16
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.920
The GAISE college report asks for

17
00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.860
real data and real questions.

18
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.950
A good project starts from a question

19
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.710
the student cares about, uses messy

20
00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:00.010
public data, and ends with a claim, its

21
00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.710
uncertainty, and its limits.

22
00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:05.010
Here is one way to spend fourteen

23
00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:08.450
weeks: four on inference, four on

24
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.510
modelling, two on causal questions, and

25
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.770
four on a staged project with a

26
00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.190
proposal, a draft and a final report.

27
00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.270
Require every submission to run from raw

28
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.770
data to final figure with one command, in

29
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.990
a notebook or script under version

30
00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:26.370
control.

31
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.890
If a marker cannot rerun it,

32
00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.390
it is not finished.

33
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.450
This also discourages copied results.

34
00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.530
Share the rubric when you set the

35
00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.250
project, not when you grade it.

36
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.080
Describe each level in words a student can

37
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.680
act on, and give feedback on the draft.

38
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.490
Hattie and Timperley show feedback

39
00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.790
works when it says where to go next.

40
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:51.750
Quick check!

41
00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.640
An outcome says students will justify

42
00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.520
the choice of a statistical model.

43
00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.100
The only assessment is a timed

44
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.580
multiple choice test of formulas.

45
00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:06.850
Is this aligned?

46
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:08.690
No.

47
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.020
Justify is the verb, and a formula

48
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.220
test cannot see a justification.

49
00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.230
A short written defence of a model

50
00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:19.590
choice on real data would measure it.

51
00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.990
In the app, open the histogram lab.

52
00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.740
Change the bin width on the same data

53
00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.640
and notice how the story changes.

54
00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.140
Use it to show students why every choice

55
00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.420
in an analysis must be justified.

56
00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:35.300
Your turn.

57
00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.310
When should students first

58
00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:38.790
see the project rubric?

59
00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.230
When the project is set.

60
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:45.030
Remember: align outcomes, activities and

61
00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.210
assessment, use real projects, require

62
00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:51.210
reproducible work, and share the rubric

63
00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:51.530
early.

64
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.110
Try it this week: take your module's

65
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.310
learning outcomes, underline each

66
00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.570
verb, and next to it write the

67
00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.910
assessment that measures it.

68
00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.950
Any verb with nothing beside

69
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.270
